{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JmmXbpw97Ath9pq1bxKyWY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough information to write a comprehensive visual gaps report. Let me analyze what I've found:\n\n**Library algorithms (src/finders/):**\n- AStarFinder\n- BestFirstFinder\n- BiAStarFinder\n- BiBestFirstFinder\n- BiBreadthFirstFinder\n- BiDijkstraFinder\n- BreadthFirstFinder\n- DijkstraFinder\n- IDAStarFinder\n- JumpPointFinder (factory that creates one of 4 variants)\n  - JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally\n  - JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle\n  - JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles\n  - JPFNeverMoveDiagonally\n\nThe UI currently only exposes A*, IDA*, and Breadth-First search, each with their own configurable parameters like heuristics, diagonal movement, bidirectional search, and corner crossing rules. I'm noticing a significant gap between what's implemented in the library and what's actually available in the visual interface.\n\nLooking at the other algorithms, Best-First, Dijkstra, and the two Jump Point Search variants are missing from the UI. Jump Point Search is hardcoded to allow diagonal movement only when there's at most one obstacle, while Orthogonal Jump Point Search never allows diagonals. The real issue is that JumpPointFinder supports four different diagonal movement modes, but the UI only shows two of them—I'm missing the \"Always\" and \"OnlyWhenNoObstacles\" variants. There's also a bug in IDA* where the heuristic isn't being set correctly. reads `$('input[name=jump_point_heuristic]:checked').val()` instead of `$('input[name=ida_heuristic]:checked').val()`. The IDA* section has `id=\"ida_heuristic\"` and radio buttons named `ida_heuristic`, but the code reads from `jump_point_heuristic`. This is a real bug.\n\nThere's also no animation speed control — `operationsPerSecond` is hardcoded at 300 with no slider for adjustment. The grid size is fixed at 64×36 without any UI to change it, and when a path isn't found, there's no visual feedback to the user. The demo lacks maze generators too, so users can only draw walls manually.\n\nJPS diagonal movement options are hardcoded instead of exposed in the UI, and there's a missing `notsupported.html` file that gets referenced when SVG isn't supported. The parent node visualization is partially implemented — the parent attribute gets captured but never rendered — and while the stats display shows path length, time, and operation count, there are other metrics that could be useful.\n\nMobile support is completely absent since only mouse events are bound, and the minified bundle might be out of sync with the source code if new pathfinding algorithms were added. Let me check if the output directory exists.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":906,"cache_read_input_tokens":34940,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":906},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d51127d4-3ec8-4e1b-bc7c-91599c878a54","uuid":"38b6da86-dbd7-4479-a0a9-5f292d95daf7"}
