{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JxFpLHiVQdGcduU297y979","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`notsupported.html` exists. Now write the report."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_read_input_tokens":37185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":251},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d51127d4-3ec8-4e1b-bc7c-91599c878a54","uuid":"52d57bf1-8279-49ea-a519-412a0c8bc974"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JxFpLHiVQdGcduU297y979","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FkUEUGmPbAYCQmBRmTcz67","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/visual-auditor/output/visual-gaps.md","content":"# Visual Auditor Report — PathFinding.js Demo\n\n## Current Visual App Capabilities\n\n### Grid\n- Fixed 64×36 node grid rendered via Raphael.js SVG\n- Draw walls: click-drag on white cells\n- Erase walls: click-drag on grey cells\n- Drag green (start) and red (end) nodes\n- Grid generates asynchronously (row-by-row) to avoid blocking browser\n\n### Controls\n- **Start Search** → runs algorithm, animates node expansion\n- **Pause Search** / **Resume Search** toggle\n- **Restart Search** during/after run\n- **Clear Walls** resets entire grid\n- **Clear Path** after finish returns to ready state\n\n### Statistics\n- Path length (rounded to 2 decimal places)\n- Time spent (ms, 4 decimal places)\n- Operation count\n\n### Algorithm Panel (accordion UI)\n| Algorithm in UI | Backed by |\n|---|---|\n| A* | `PF.AStarFinder` / `PF.BiAStarFinder` |\n| IDA* | `PF.IDAStarFinder` |\n| Breadth-First Search | `PF.BreadthFirstFinder` / `PF.BiBreadthFirstFinder` |\n| Best-First Search | `PF.BestFirstFinder` / `PF.BiBestFirstFinder` |\n| Dijkstra | `PF.DijkstraFinder` / `PF.BiDijkstraFinder` |\n| Jump Point Search | `PF.JumpPointFinder` (IfAtMostOneObstacle) |\n| Orthogonal Jump Point Search | `PF.JumpPointFinder` (Never diagonal) |\n\n### Node Color Legend\n- White → normal/unvisited\n- Grey → wall/blocked\n- Green → start node\n- Orange-red → end node\n- Light green (`#98fb98`) → opened (frontier)\n- Pale cyan (`#afeeee`) → closed (visited)\n- Light grey (`#e5e5e5`) → tested (IDA*/JPS recursion)\n- Yellow line → final path\n\n---\n\n## Algorithms Available vs Missing from UI\n\n### Library exports (`src/PathFinding.js`)\n```\nAStarFinder         ✅ exposed\nBestFirstFinder     ✅ exposed\nBreadthFirstFinder  ✅ exposed\nDijkstraFinder      ✅ exposed\nBiAStarFinder       ✅ exposed (via bi-directional checkbox)\nBiBestFirstFinder   ✅ exposed (via bi-directional checkbox)\nBiBreadthFirstFinder ✅ exposed (via bi-directional checkbox)\nBiDijkstraFinder    ✅ exposed (via bi-directional checkbox)\nIDAStarFinder       ✅ exposed\nJumpPointFinder     ⚠️  PARTIAL — only 2 of 4 diagonal modes exposed\n```\n\n### JumpPointFinder Diagonal Modes (4 total, 2 exposed)\n| Mode | DiagonalMovement const | UI label | Exposed? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| IfAtMostOneObstacle | `3` | \"Jump Point Search\" | ✅ |\n| Never | `2` | \"Orthogonal Jump Point Search\" | ✅ |\n| Always | `1` | — | ❌ **Missing** |\n| OnlyWhenNoObstacles | `4` | — | ❌ **Missing** |\n\n---\n\n## UI/UX Gaps and Broken Features\n\n### Bug — IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\n**File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\n```js\n// BUG: reads jump_point_heuristic instead of ida_heuristic\nheuristic = $('input[name=jump_point_heuristic]:checked').val();\n```\nShould be `$('input[name=ida_heuristic]:checked').val()`. Currently IDA* always uses whichever heuristic is selected in the JPS panel (or falls back to undefined → likely Manhattan as first checked). Selecting Euclidean/Octile/Chebyshev in the IDA* section has no effect.\n\n### Gap — No animation speed control\n`operationsPerSecond` is hardcoded at `300` in `controller.js:95`. No UI slider. Users can't slow down to study behavior or speed up for large searches.\n\n### Gap — Fixed grid size\nGrid locked to 64×36. No UI input to change dimensions. Larger grids would stress-test performance; smaller grids help educational demos.\n\n### Gap — No \"path not found\" feedback\nWhen `finder.findPath()` returns an empty array, `View.drawPath()` returns silently (`visual/js/view.js:245`). User sees no indication that no path exists — the UI just finishes with stats showing `length: 0`.\n\n### Gap — No maze / pattern generators\nWalls must be drawn manually. Common demo features absent:\n- Random maze (recursive division, Prim's, DFS)\n- Recursive subdivision\n- Random scatter\n- Clear all walls button exists but no generate button\n\n### Gap — Parent edge not visualized\n`view.js:170` has a TODO comment:\n```js\ncase 'parent':\n    // XXX: Maybe draw a line from this node to its parent?\n    // This would be expensive.\n    break;\n```\nParent relationships captured in operations but never rendered. Showing parent arrows would clarify how algorithms build their search tree.\n\n### Gap — JPS diagonal mode not selectable\nBoth JPS entries hardcode their `diagonalMovement` value. The 4 available modes are not exposed via a dropdown or radio group. User cannot switch between `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` at all.\n\n### Gap — No touch/mobile support\nOnly mouse events (`mousedown`, `mousemove`, `mouseup`) are bound. No touch event handlers. Demo unusable on tablets/phones.\n\n### Gap — No grid import/export\nNo way to save or load a wall configuration. Users must redraw obstacles each session.\n\n### Gap — Weight spinner available for IDA* but uses duplicate name attribute\n`panel.js` reads `$('#ida_section input[name=astar_weight]').val()` — the IDA* weight spinner has `name=\"astar_weight\"`, same as A* section. DOM queries are scoped by section so this works, but it's fragile and misleading.\n\n### Gap — No comparison / multi-algorithm run\nCan only run one algorithm at a time. No side-by-side comparison or stats table across runs.\n\n### Gap — Speed/operations slider not wired to slider widget\n`jquery.ui.slider.min.js` is loaded but no slider widget is instantiated in the UI. The library is unused dead weight.\n\n---\n\n## Suggested Visual Test Scenarios\n\n### 1. Basic path exists — all algorithms\n**Setup:** Open grid, default start/end positions, no walls  \n**Expected:** All algorithms find a path; path rendered in yellow; stats show non-zero length and operation count\n\n### 2. No path exists\n**Setup:** Surround start node completely with walls  \n**Expected:** Clear user-facing message \"No path found\" (currently broken — silent)\n\n### 3. IDA* heuristic selection bug\n**Setup:** Select IDA*, pick Euclidean heuristic in IDA* panel, run  \n**Expected:** Should use Euclidean (currently uses JPS heuristic selection — bug at `panel.js:160`)\n\n### 4. Bi-directional vs unidirectional comparison\n**Setup:** Same grid, run A* unidirectional then bi-directional  \n**Expected:** Bi-directional explores fewer nodes (lower operation count); same or similar path\n\n### 5. Jump Point Search — diagonal modes\n**Setup:** Grid with scattered walls, run \"Jump Point Search\" vs \"Orthogonal Jump Point Search\"  \n**Expected:** JPS allows diagonal moves; Orthogonal restricts to cardinal only — paths differ in shape\n\n### 6. Weight parameter effect on A*\n**Setup:** Run A* with weight=1 vs weight=5 on same grid  \n**Expected:** Higher weight → fewer operations (greedier) but potentially suboptimal path length\n\n### 7. IDA* time limit\n**Setup:** Dense wall grid, set time limit to 1 second, run IDA*  \n**Expected:** IDA* aborts at time limit; some form of feedback shown\n\n### 8. Animation at boundary conditions\n**Setup:** Start and end nodes adjacent (1 step apart)  \n**Expected:** Minimal animation, path length ~1, fast finish\n\n### 9. Start equals end\n**Setup:** Drag end node onto start node  \n**Expected:** No crash; zero-length path or graceful no-op\n\n### 10. Drag start/end during search\n**Setup:** Begin search, attempt to drag start/end while animating  \n**Expected:** State machine should block drag (only allowed in `ready`/`finished` states) — verify no crash or silent state corruption\n\n### 11. Wall on start or end position\n**Setup:** Programmatically (or via racing) place wall on start node  \n**Expected:** Graceful failure, not crash\n\n### 12. Full grid walls (no walkable cells)\n**Setup:** Clear and draw walls everywhere  \n**Expected:** Robust no-path handling; no JS errors\n\n### 13. Large operation count performance\n**Setup:** Run Dijkstra or BFS on open 64×36 grid with start top-left, end bottom-right  \n**Expected:** Many operations; animation remains smooth at 300 ops/sec; no frame drops or JS timeout\n\n### 14. Pause / Resume cycle\n**Setup:** Start search, pause mid-animation, resume  \n**Expected:** Animation continues from exact paused state; no duplicate or skipped operations\n\n### 15. Restart during search\n**Setup:** Start search, click Restart before finish  \n**Expected:** Animation clears, new search begins cleanly; no stale colored nodes remain\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_read_input_tokens":37185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":251},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d51127d4-3ec8-4e1b-bc7c-91599c878a54","uuid":"45a1bb82-046d-416d-b801-57af735d428f"}
